LESSON 13: ADD GROCERY FORM
================================================================================
PART 1: OVERVIEW OF THE LESSON
================================================================================

WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS LESSON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This lesson focuses on creating a reusable form for adding grocery items to
the Grocery List App.

You will understand:

• Creating an AddGroceryForm component

• Managing multiple controlled inputs

• Handling text, number, and select controls

• Validating form values

• Displaying field-level errors

• Calculating a live line-cost preview

• Handling form submission

• Normalizing submitted values

• Resetting the controlled form

• Passing submitted data to a parent component

• Adding a new item to grocery-list state

• Connecting the form, list, and item components

• Providing accessible user feedback


WHY THIS LESSON IS IMPORTANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Grocery List currently displays and manages existing items.

The Add Grocery Form introduces the create operation:

USER ENTERS DATA
        ↓
FORM STATE
        ↓
VALIDATION
        ↓
NORMALIZATION
        ↓
NEW GROCERY ITEM
        ↓
PARENT CALLBACK
        ↓
GROCERY LIST STATE
        ↓
UPDATED LIST


The same pattern is used in:

• Todo forms

• Product forms

• Contact forms

• Expense forms

• Inventory forms

• Order-entry forms

• Task-creation forms


