================================================================================
HTML CONSTRAINTS VS APPLICATION VALIDATION
================================================================================

HTML provides constraints such as:

min="1"

max="999"

step="1"


Application validation also checks the values.

Why both?

HTML constraints:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Browser-level guidance

• Useful native behavior


Application validation:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Application-specific error messages

• Explicit business-rule processing

• Consistent validation logic


Server-side validation is still required if data is sent to a backend.


================================================================================
PRICE DECIMAL NOTE
================================================================================

The input uses:

step="0.01"


This guides the user toward two-decimal increments.

However, a production currency model may require more deliberate handling.

Common approaches include:

• Store minor currency units as integers

  Example:

  $3.99
      ↓
  399 cents


• Use a decimal-safe money type in the backend


JavaScript floating-point values can produce precision surprises in some
calculations.


For this learning application:

Number + toFixed(2)


is acceptable for display-oriented practice.


================================================================================
ERROR CLEARING
================================================================================

This lesson clears the old error when the user changes that field.

Example:

errors.quantity:

'Quantity must be at least 1'


User changes Quantity.


Then:

errors.quantity

becomes:

''


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Clearing an error does not prove that the new value is valid.

Alternative strategies:

• Revalidate on change

• Validate on blur

• Validate again on submission


The chosen behavior should be consistent.


